tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-2452-a-private-module-with-its-brackets-forgotten-is-told-once.case/main.hero:6:5: error[package_unmarked]: there is no module `core/internal/scan` of this program, and `core` is an entry of its catalogue: a package's module is written in angle brackets, and `use <core>/internal/scan` would name a module private to `<core>`: a module whose path holds `internal` as a part after its first, a folder's name or its own, is named only by the module the path before the last such part names and by the modules under it; name what `<core>` offers instead
